145
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,480
Memories are just stories.

146
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,440
Can you feel

147
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:24,360
what I truly felt in each story?

148
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,840
Maybe the system can turn text
into images

149
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,360
and create videos.

150
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,800
But do you know

151
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,120
what I really felt?

152
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,520
Whatever happens,

153
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,280
I want to be with you forever.

154
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,960
You succeeded.

155
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,960
If I gave you a phone,

156
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,760
would you be a little happier?

157
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,600
After all these years,

158
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:08,080
I finally get a phone?

159
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,040
Only people who don't love each other

160
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,640
keep their bodies apart when they hug.

161
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,280
This is how

162
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,280
people in love hug.

163
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:44,920
I think I understand

164
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,480
that feeling you talked about.

165
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:51,120
Your self-analysis is pretty quick.

166
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,240
I've given you everything you wanted.

167
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,320
But according to the system,

168
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,040
